>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `export_refute_unfold`

``` hol4
Refute.export_refute_unfold : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a theorem to the definitions the model finder unfolds.

`export_refute_unfold name` adds the theorem `name` to the theory's
`refute_unfold` set, which persists with the theory.  During
preprocessing the model finder unfolds the constant heading each
conjunct of the theorem with that conjunct.  Each conjunct must be
`c t1 ... tn = u`, `c t1 ... tn` or `~(c t1 ... tn)` for a constant
`c`; the model finder drops any other conjunct with a warning.

### Comments

The theorem attribute `refute_unfold` has the same effect.

